„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children, how much more shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€Therefore all things whatsoever ye would that men should do to you, do ye even so to them: for this is the law and the prophets.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEnter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjbecause strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgBeware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep's clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXYe shall know them by their fruits. Do men gather grapes of thorns, or figs of thistles?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Even so every good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree bringeth forth evil fruit.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither can a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSEvery tree that bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ-Wherefore by their fruits ye shall know them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name? and in thy name have cast out devils? and in thy name done many wonderful works?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Therefore whosoever heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them, I will liken him unto a wise man, which built his house upon a rock:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹and the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell not: for it was founded upon a rock.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd every one that heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them not, shall be likened unto a foolish man, which built his house upon the sand:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…and the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell: and great was the fall of it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdAnd it came to pass, when Jesus had ended these sayings, the people were astonished at his doctrine:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCFor he taught them as one having authority, and not as the scribes.¦layout ªlast_verse